<ArticleLayout
  title="Circular Economy & Waste-to-Value"
  description="Plastic recycling, biogas, pottery, mycelium materials and coastal waste projects across Sierra Leone, Zimbabwe and The Gambia."
>
  <p>
    Waste is a resource in the wrong place. This programme area turns
    material that would otherwise be burned, dumped or left in coastal
    waters into income, jobs and cleaner communities.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    Community-scale plastic recycling projects, now running in Sierra
    Leone with country-specific tracks under development for Zimbabwe
    and The Gambia, turn plastic waste into a circular social
    enterprise.
  </p>
  <p>
    A community biogas and waste-to-energy pilot converts organic waste
    into usable energy. A pottery enterprise hub gives makers firing
    access and entrepreneurship training around ClayWorks production. A
    mycelium innovation pilot, MycoLoop, explores mushroom-based
    packaging and building materials, with a potential livelihood
    strand around mushroom cultivation. A septic and solid-waste
    project, built around community ownership, addresses waste and
    public health together on the coast.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Each project pairs a local implementing partner, who runs the
    operation and hires locally, with donor coordination, monitoring
    and learning support from Ayara&rsquo;s side. That keeps projects
    grounded in what a community can actually run and maintain, while
    still meeting the documentation funders expect.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
